msgid ""
"Return True if this addon is in Expansion Mode (discoverable by Sanctus Library).\n"
"\n"
"Only relevant for clones with ENABLE_EXPANSIONS=False (e.g. Sanctus Viz).\n"
"When True, the addon's panels/tools are suppressed and only its assets\n"
"are exposed to Sanctus Library.\n"
"\n"
"This is read at register() time. It checks the PERSISTENT sentinel file\n"
"(stored via bpy.utils.extension_path_user) rather than the preference,\n"
"because Blender restores preferences AFTER register() runs. The sentinel\n"
"is written when the user toggles Expansion Mode ON in the preferences,\n"
"and survives Blender restarts — so register() can reliably detect the\n"
"mode without depending on preference-restore timing."
msgstr "Return True if this addon is in Expansion Mode (discoverable by Sanctus Library). Only relevant for clones with ENABLE_EXPANSIONS=False (e.g. Sanctus Viz). When True, the addon's panels/tools are suppressed and only its assets are exposed to Sanctus Library. This is read at register() time. It checks the PERSISTENT sentinel file (stored via bpy.utils.extension_path_user) rather than the preference, because Blender restores preferences AFTER register() runs. The sentinel is written when the user toggles Expansion Mode ON in the preferences, and survives Blender restarts — so register() can reliably detect the mode without depending on preference-restore timing."

