msgid ""
"Dependency management for Sanctus Core.\n"
"\n"
"This module contains ALL dependency install/repair logic (Pillow, resvg-py).\n"
"\n"
"It is deliberately kept FREE of any import of `t3dn_bip` (or anything that\n"
"transitively imports PIL/resvg). That is critical: `__init__.py` must call\n"
"`_prepare_syspath()` BEFORE any module that imports PIL/resvg is loaded, so\n"
"that `sanctus_deps` is on `sys.path` before `t3dn_bip` tries to import PIL.\n"
"\n"
"If these helpers lived in `operators/library.py`, importing them would pull in\n"
"`t3dn_bip.ops` (which imports PIL) BEFORE `_prepare_syspath` ran, producing a\n"
"cascade of \"No module named 'PIL'\" errors for every icon."
msgstr "Dependency management for Sanctus Core. This module contains ALL dependency install/repair logic (Pillow, resvg-py). It is deliberately kept FREE of any import of `t3dn_bip` (or anything that transitively imports PIL/resvg). That is critical: `__init__.py` must call `_prepare_syspath()` BEFORE any module that imports PIL/resvg is loaded, so that `sanctus_deps` is on `sys.path` before `t3dn_bip` tries to import PIL. If these helpers lived in `operators/library.py`, importing them would pull in `t3dn_bip.ops` (which imports PIL) BEFORE `_prepare_syspath` ran, producing a cascade of \"No module named 'PIL'\" errors for every icon."

msgid "Return the dedicated user-writable install folder for dependencies."
msgstr "Return the dedicated user-writable install folder for dependencies."

msgid ""
"Return a real Python interpreter path for pip installs.\n"
"\n"
"- On Windows, Blender's ``sys.executable`` IS the bundled python.exe.\n"
"- On macOS/Linux it can be the Blender binary itself, which cannot run\n"
"  ``-m pip``. ``bpy.app.binary_path_python`` was REMOVED in Blender 5.2\n"
"  (verified: AttributeError), so we locate the bundled interpreter next\n"
"  to the Blender binary using the standard layout:\n"
"    macOS:   <Blender.app>/Contents/Resources/<ver>/python/bin/python3.x\n"
"    Linux:   <blender_dir>/<ver>/python/bin/python3.x"
msgstr "Return a real Python interpreter path for pip installs. - On Windows, Blender's ``sys.executable`` IS the bundled python.exe. - On macOS/Linux it can be the Blender binary itself, which cannot run ``-m pip``. ``bpy.app.binary_path_python`` was REMOVED in Blender 5.2 (verified: AttributeError), so we locate the bundled interpreter next to the Blender binary using the standard layout: macOS:   <Blender.app>/Contents/Resources/<ver>/python/bin/python3.x Linux:   <blender_dir>/<ver>/python/bin/python3.x"

